<<<
This common idiom, which looks illogical (of all I know being the logical form) is no doubt defensible as a development or survival of the archaic Caesar, the greatest traveller,(of a prince, that had ever been. ere means in the way of, & we should now write for instead of it.
===
This common idiom, which looks illogical (*of all I know* being the logical form) is no doubt defensible as a development or survival of the archaic type *Caesar, the greatest traveller, of a prince, that had ever been.* *Of* there means *in the way of*, & we should now write *for* instead of it.
>>>

